{
  "_comment": [
    "SPARK — S167: atlas specs for the SIX TIER-9 BOSSES, four states each.",
    "",
    "⭐ THE TIER-3 UNIT PATTERN, because a boss is a CHARACTER (actions) and not a structure",
    "(conditions): framesPerState 12, every state a veo `clip`, and normaliseStateScale ON.",
    "",
    "⭐ cellW/cellH 320, NOT the units' 200. A boss must READ as bigger than the army around it, and",
    "the cell is the budget the union bounding box is fitted into — a boss authored at 200 would be",
    "matted and scaled to exactly the same on-screen height as a tier-3 bat, because",
    "GOBLIN_SPRITE_BASE_SCALE is a single global applied to every atlas-backed creature and there is",
    "no per-type scale lookup. The cell is therefore the ONLY lever that makes a boss look like one,",
    "and 320/200 = 1.6x.",
    "",
    "⚠ normaliseStateScale IS set here, where the tower specs deliberately do NOT set it. It equalises",
    "the SEED-FRAME size across states, which is exactly right when four CLIPS of one character",
    "disagree about zoom — veo frames the same boss differently between idle and attack, and without",
    "this the boss visibly grows and shrinks as he changes state. The towers are four separate",
    "DRAWINGS of a building whose size legitimately changes, which is the opposite case.",
    "",
    "⚠ enclosedWhiteLimitPct 4e-05, set EXPLICITLY. The builder's default is 0.003 — 75x looser — and",
    "taking that default by omission is precisely the S165 defect the owner reported by eye. A boss is",
    "a CHARACTER, so the limit is protecting eyes and glints here rather than being free; 4e-05 is the",
    "value the tier-3 units were tuned to after measurement, and these are the same subject class.",
    "",
    "⚠ `die` IS BUILT EVEN THOUGH NO RENDERER ARM CAN REQUEST ROW 3. goblinRenderer.syncSprite maps",
    "every FSM state to attack/walk/idle, so the die row is unreachable today — the same state the",
    "tier-3 units ship in. It is built now because the clip exists now."
  ],
